      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-06-20_WidnesExaminer_art0061" n="art0061">
        <head>EVERY PERSON'S FUTURE.</head>
        <p>EVERY PERSON'S FUTURE.</p>
        <p>Every person's future is, to a certain extent, in hi. own hand. Many a future which might have been bril liant has been darkened by lack of the spirit of self-help Many a home might have been gladdened by life and health and comfort, has been saddened by poverty, illness and death, in many cases wholly preventible. The spring and summer months are, from a sanitary point of view, among the most important of the year. Due care may now mean a healthy and happy ScIMITICr and autumn, and robust constitution to meet the trials of next winter. Neglect may now mean a joyless sum- mer, a trying autumn, and a broken constitution to succumb under the attacks of any exceptional trial. There are indeed few that do not feel the system needs recruiting. With some it is " only a little cough," " tendency to bronchitis," and others, " not quite up to the mark," " a sort of aIZ over sinking feeling," " tog weak to do anything about the house," " these recurrind headaches,"" no appetite for his food," &amp;c. These an a dozen others are common expressions which all point to the urgent need of same good tonic. What change of air can do for you in a few months' time—if you are nr, worse then than you are now—a course of some good tonic mixture, a reliable medicine of established reputa- tion and of prov€4.l virtue will do now. There are several tonic mixtures to be had, but none which have been so uniformly successful as Gwilym Evans Quinine Bitters, the Vegetable Tonic.</p>
        <p>It is the Best REMEDY of the age for</p>
        <p>WEAKNESS, NERVOUSNESS,</p>
        <p>LOW SPIRITS,</p>
        <p>MELANCHOLY,</p>
        <p>CHEST AFFECTION, LOSS OF APPETITE, INDIGESTION, AND BLOOD DISORDERS. At this season of the year no one should be without GWILYM EVANS' QUININE BITTERS. A course taken now will be valuable in giving tone to the system, new life to the blood, and in bracing tha nerves. Praised by everybody. Avoid Imitations. See the name " Gwilym Evans" on the Label, Stamp and Bottle. Prices :—Bottles, 2s. 91 ; double size. 4s. 6d. To be had of all Chemists, or direct from the Proprietors : QUININE BITTERS MANUFACTURING Co., LTD., LLANELLY. SOUTH WILES.</p>
