        <p>WARRINGTON TECHNICAL INSTITUTE</p>
        <p>RESULTS OF EXAMINATION. The results of the examination under tee Union:oi Lancashire and Cheshire Institutes of the Continuation School and Commercial Classes are now to hand. The following is a list of the successful candidates : ARlTlMlSTlC—(Elernentary) First Class : J. Basker- ville, J. Fowler, P. B. Gandy. J. Gorst, E. Kendrick, Annie Owen, .1. Peers, Agnes Richardson, Mary Richard- son. Mary Ward, G. A. Williams. Second Class: B. Baker, Georgina Barlow, W. J. Barlow, W. Bennett, Martha Berry, F. Bullen, J. A. Carpenter.W. Carpenter Sarah Costelloe, W. Critchley, Catherine Daley, Mary F Darton, J. Hawthorn, T. J. Hopkins, E. Lancaster, T. Mc Whirter, C. Mason J. Mason, Edith Maybury, A. F. Pickford, G. F. Rice, Rimmer, J. M. Shaw, G. E. Strange, Edith Turner, W. Wakefield, J. L. Warburton. (Senior Commercial).—First class, with distinction : H. S. Knowles.—Third ciass H. P. Bate, J. E. Knowles. (Junior Commercial).—First class: A. T. Charnock, Esther McGarty. Second class : G. W. R. Baines, J. I. Carpenter, D. B. Clarke, G. T. Fern. C. Horobin,. Emily Houghton, C. H. Longshaw, A. ?arr. H. Wood. fhird class; W. Hopkins, Florence McGarty, J. S. Tilling. BOOKSISPING.—First Class with distinction: T. P. Rathbone. First Class: .1. S. Bate. J. F. Melbourne, F. G. R. Wood. Second Class: C. H. Longshaw, H. Sum- ner. Third Class: .T. S. Craik, W. Daintith, R. H. Evans. I. W. Eyre, G. Harding, F. H. Hollingsworth, F. Jones, S. Payne, J. S. Tilling. lIANDWRITING.—.FIIIt Class with distinction: J. S. Bate. Fir at Class: H. Sumner, G. A. Williams. Second Class: A. Horebin, M. W. LOGlcrbShaW, Esther H. McGarty. Third Class: R. Forster, Florence McGarty. ENGLISH (Elementary).—First Class: D. B. Clarke, Mary Lea, Edith Turner, Mary Ward. Second Class: Georgina Barlow, Sarah Costelloe, Mary F. Darton„ E. Lancaster, Bertha London, A. F. Pickford. Margaret Raftery. (Commercial).—Second Class :J. D. Owen, T. P. Rathbone. Music (Elementary).—Second Class : Ethel Ribbed, E. L. Pearce, H. A. Roberts, J. Williamson. Third Class: E. W. Gandy, J. E. Hannan. COOKERY (Elementary).—First Class.with distinction : Mary Ward. First Class: Florence McGarty. Second Class : Elsie A. Bailey, Matilda Berry,Emily Houghtoo. Third Class : Lilian Flay ward. SHORTHAND (Speed).—Second Class ; E. W. Kirk. Third Class: P. W. Boardinan, J. I. Carpenter. R. Car- penter, J. T. Gordon, H. Greene, H. Havieur. J. S. Til- ling. 11. Wallington. (Elementary) Pass : B. Baker,D. B. Clarke, A. Horobin, W. Rieby, F. White. SPANISH (Commercial).—Second Class : F, Sirncock. Third Class : E. W. Jones. DRESSMAKING.—First Class: Ethel Ashton, Elizabeth Blease, Mary J. Carpenter. Eva Critchley„ Mrs. Gleave, Sarah Handford, Kate Mantle, Alison S. May, Amy Osborne' Annie F. Wallington. Second Class Mabel Clive, Clara B. Dale, Mary Evans, Elizabeth Fairclough, Ethel Fry, Emily Jordan, Mrs. Lowe, Mabel E Pearce. Third Class : Mary Ward. Nescinkwoak (Intermediate).—Socond Class: Sarah E. aerobia, Esther McGarty, Florence McGarry. (Ele- mentary) First Class : Georgina Mt now, Clara D aven- port,Matilda Gartland. Second Class Clytie Appleton, Elizabeth E. Hugh, Edith Maybary, Ethel Mounfield, Fanny Mounfield, Florence Tonke. Third Class :Eva A. Tilling. Flaxen (Literary).—Second Class : May Hilton. Third Class : Nellie Fowler. (Elementary) First Class :E. W. Kirk, E. E. Lowe. Third Class Mary J. Carpenter, Gwynneth Corney, Clara Harding, G. Harding, Susan Jones.</p>
        <p>_ DRAWING.—The Continuation School Was examined in drawing by the Science and Art Department, the general result being an award of " Excellent " for the teaching as a whole, which carries the highest grant, whilst the follawin7 pupils obtained Cards of Merit F. Baker, J. J. Baskerville, R. G. Brandreth, F. Bullen,W. Carpenter, R. Foster, P. B. Gandy, J. L. Hawthorn, J. Hill, E. Kendrick, Bertha London, Ella C. London,Mary Lea, T. McWhirter, C. Mason, P. Sexton, John N. Ver- non, J. L. Warburton, Mary B. Ward.</p>
